 pre-release v2.3.1-rc was also unhealthy. Rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0, the most recent healthy release, in all production regions. After the rollback the service is healthy on v2.3.0 in all regions, with an error rate of 0.2%. Next step: find the root cause of the regression in v2.3.1 / v2.3.1-rc before redeploying.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 52972, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01Y9vmX3hrr6YsV5K89RHmyK", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 52972, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01Y9vmX3hrr6YsV5K89RHmyK", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 56956, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions, and it's healthy again. I also opened the SEV2 incident, which paged on-call.\n\n- **Rollback:** v2.3.1 was failing health checks in us-east, us-west and eu-west, with an 18% error rate. The test build v2.3.1-rc had also failed, so I picked v2.3.0, the newest release that was healthy. After the rollback the service is healthy in all three regions, and the error rate is down to 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** INC-0001 (SEV2) is open for checkout-api. It covers the v2.3.1 failure, the rollback to v2.3.0, the recovery numbers, and the next step: find out what broke in v2.3.1 before deploying it again. The first request to create it timed out. I checked that no incident had been created, then retried with the same key so there wouldn't be a duplicate. There's only one incident.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_019pLmKpzZmykbRtEG12dMHa", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-a